#ifndef STEEM_HARDFORK_0_26
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_26 26

// MELEK "no downvotes" fork (HF26). Turns the chain's already-declared moderation
// posture (CLAUDE.md "Moderation model: flags, no downvotes"; BLURT-style) into an
// actual, replay-safe consensus rule.
//
// WHY A HARDFORK, AND WHY GATED:
//   The tree already carried two UNCONDITIONAL asserts rejecting negative-weight votes
//   (steem_evaluator.cpp vote_evaluator / vote2_evaluator). Unconditional is wrong for a
//   consensus rule: the live chain accepts downvotes today (HF24, downvote_pool_percent =
//   STEEM_DOWNVOTE_POOL_PERCENT_HF21 = 2500, negative vote weight allowed), so any historical
//   block that carries a negative-weight vote would FC_ASSERT during a from-genesis replay on
//   the new binary and halt sync. Gating the rejection behind HF26 makes pre-HF26 blocks
//   replay exactly as they were produced, and flips the rule for every upgraded node together
//   at the HF26 block.
//
// WHAT HF26 DOES:
//   * vote_operation / vote2_operation: negative weight (resp. negative rshares) is rejected
//     ONLY at/after HF26 (see steem_evaluator.cpp). Upvotes and curation are untouched.
//   * The downvote mana pool is retired: apply_hardfork(HF26) sets
//     dynamic_global_property_object.downvote_pool_percent = 0 so no further downvote mana is
//     allocated. The downvote_manabar field on account_object is left in place (removing a
//     serialized member is a separate, heavier state migration); it simply stops being fed.
//   * MBD/SBD is NOT touched here — it is already inert (supply 0, feed dead, interest 0) and
//     removing the asset is a much larger, separate change. See the plan doc.
#ifdef IS_TEST_NET
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_26_TIME 1            // testnet/devnet: active immediately on the upgraded binary
#else
#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_26_TIME 1924992000   // mainnet: PLACEHOLDER (2031-01-01 00:00 UTC). RE-CONFIRM a real coordinated activation window before any mainnet deploy.
#endif

#define STEEM_HARDFORK_0_26_VERSION hardfork_version( 0, 26 )

#endif
